      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Within an inherited inversion formula, integration by parts replaces divergent factorwise integrals of logarithms by integrable logarithmic-derivative terms. A generic factor log(1-s/β) then contributes different branch-dependent integrals according to β's half-plane, and the source carefully chooses paths so the integration constants disappear; however, this slice never defines f(x) or supplies the preceding factorization.",
